[9.195817, "o", "cified by the variable obase. The legal\r\n302:            values for  obase are 2 through BC_BASE_MAX.  (See the section\r\n305:            character digit method of printing the numbers where each higher\r\n306:            base digit is printed as a base 10 number.  The multi-character\r\n308:            characters required to represent the base ten value of \"obase-1\".\r\n310:            printable on a single output line.  These long numbers will be\r\n312:            The maximum number of characters printed per line is 70.  Due to\r\n313:            the interactive nature of bc, printing a number causes the side\r\n314:            effect of assigning the printed value to the special variable\r\n315:            last. This allows the user to recover the last value printed\r\n316:            without having to retype the expression that printed the number.\r\n317:            Assigning to last is legal and will overwrite the last printed\r\n319:            remain until the next number is printed or another value is\r\n324:     string Th"]
[9.19585, "o", "e string is printed to the output.  Strings start with a double\r\n327:            newline.  No newline character is printed after the string.\r\n329:     print list\r\n330:            The print statement (an extension) provides another method of\r\n332:            by commas.  Each string or expression is printed in the order of\r\n333:            the list.  No terminating newline is printed.  Expressions are\r\n334:            evaluated and their value is printed and assigned to the variable\r\n335:            last. Strings in the print statement are printed to the output and\r\n382:     continue\r\n383:            The continue statement (an extension)  causes the most recent\r\n417:     is undefined until a definition is encountered in the input.  That\r\n420:     definition.  A function is defined as follows:\r\n421:            define name ( parameters ) { newline\r\n422:                auto_list   statement_list }\r\n425:     Parameters are numbers or arrays (an extension).  In the function\r\n426:     definition, zero or more paramet"]
[9.195872, "o", "ers are defined by listing their names\r\n430:     for number parameters.  The same notation is used for passing arrays as\r\n431:     for defining array parameters.  The named array is passed by value to the\r\n435:     also occur for the call to an undefined function.\r\n437:     The auto_list is an optional list of variables that are for \"local\" use.\r\n438:     The syntax of the auto list (if present) is \"auto name, ... ;\".  (The\r\n439:     semicolon is optional.)  Each name is the name of an auto variable.\r\n445:     these variables are restored.  The parameters are really auto variables\r\n448:     function A calls function B, B may access function A's auto variables by\r\n449:     just using the same name, unless function B has called them auto\r\n450:     variables.  Due to the fact that auto variables and parameters are pushed\r\n463:     Functions also change the usage of the variable ibase.  All constants in\r\n464:     the function body will be converted using the value of ibase at the time\r\n465:     of the function ca"]
