[9.195894, "o", "\r\n504:     default scale is set to 20.   The math functions will calculate their\r\n505:     results to the scale set at the time of their call.  The math library\r\n506:     defines the following functions:\r\n524:             pi=$(echo \"scale=10; 4*a(1)\" | bc -l)\r\n528:            scale = 20\r\n535:            define e(x) {\r\n536:              auto  a, d, e, f, i, m, v, z\r\n545:              z = scale;\r\n546:              scale = 4 + z + .44*x;\r\n561:                  scale = z\r\n573:            scale=2\r\n574:            print \"\\nCheck book program!\\n\"\r\n575:            print \"  Remember, deposits are negative transactions.\\n\"\r\n576:            print \"  Exit by a 0 transaction.\\n\\n\"\r\n578:            print \"Initial balance? \"; bal = read()\r\n580:            print \"\\n\"\r\n591:            define f (x) {\r\n630:            variables and arrays.  They have been extended to be multi-\r\n660:     print statement\r\n661:            POSIX bc does not have a print statement .\r\n663:     continue statement\r\n664:            POSIX bc does not hav"]
[9.195904, "o", "e a continue statement.\r\n669:     array parameters\r\n670:            POSIX bc does not (currently) support array parameters in full.\r\n671:            The POSIX grammar allows for arrays in function definitions, but\r\n672:            does not provide a method to specify an array as an actual\r\n674:            Traditional implementations of bc have only call by value array\r\n678:            POSIX bc requires the opening brace on the same line as the define\r\n679:            key word and the auto statement on the next line.\r\n683:            to be defined.  This version may allow these \"old style\"\r\n699:            statement and continue to parse the function.  Once a syntax error\r\n701:            becomes undefined.  Syntax errors in the interactive execution\r\n720:            message will be printed to notify the user that bc is ready for\r\n721:            more input.  All previously defined functions remain defined and\r\n722:            the value of all non-auto variables are the value at the point of\r\n723:            i"]
